/-!
# The binary octahedral subgroup of SU(2)

In unit-quaternion coordinates the **binary octahedral group** of order 48 is obtained by adjoining
to the 24 Hurwitz units of the binary tetrahedral group (`TauCeti.SU2.binaryTetrahedralSubgroup`)
the 24 unit quaternions

* `(±1 ± i) / √2`, `(±1 ± j) / √2`, `(±1 ± k) / √2`, `(±i ± j) / √2`, `(±i ± k) / √2`, and
  `(±j ± k) / √2`,

that is, the unit quaternions with exactly two nonzero coordinates, both equal to `±1 / √2`
(`TauCeti.SU2.mem_binaryOctahedralSubgroup_iff_coords`).

This file records the 24 new points by their `√2`-scaled integer coordinates, the finite set
`TauCeti.SU2.binaryOctahedralCosetCoords` of vectors in `{-1, 0, 1}⁴` with exactly two nonzero
entries (`TauCeti.SU2.mem_binaryOctahedralCosetCoords_iff_card`), equivalently the integer
solutions of `v₀² + v₁² + v₂² + v₃² = 2` (`TauCeti.SU2.mem_binaryOctahedralCosetCoords_iff`), and
constructs the binary octahedral subgroup of the native matrix group `SU(2)` as the union of
`TauCeti.SU2.binaryTetrahedralSubgroup` with the matrices of `(v₀ + v₁ i + v₂ j + v₃ k) / √2`
under `Quaternion.toComplexMatrix`. Equivalently, an element of `SU(2)` lies in the subgroup
exactly when its quaternion coordinates lie either in `(1 / 2) ℤ⁴` or in `(1 / √2) ℤ⁴`
(`TauCeti.SU2.mem_binaryOctahedralSubgroup_iff_exists_int`).

Two arithmetic facts underlie the construction:

* **Disjointness**: no point of `binaryTetrahedralSubgroup` has `(1 / √2)`-scaled integer
  coordinates, because `√2` is irrational and every coset vector has a nonzero coordinate.
* **Closure under multiplication**: multiplying two `(1 / √2)`-scaled integer quaternions clears
  the denominator `(√2)² = 2` to give half-integer coordinates, hence a Hurwitz unit; multiplying
  a doubled Hurwitz coordinate vector `v` (whose four entries share a parity) by a `√2`-scaled
  vector `w` (whose four entries have even sum) produces an integer quaternion with four even
  entries, which halves back into `(1 / √2) ℤ⁴`.

The two 24-element pieces therefore form a group of exact order 48
(`TauCeti.SU2.binaryOctahedralCoordsEquiv`, `TauCeti.SU2.natCard_binaryOctahedralSubgroup`) in
which the binary tetrahedral subgroup has index two and is consequently normal. The rotation
generator `r = TauCeti.SU2.binaryDihedralRotation 4 = (1 + i) / √2` of the binary dihedral group of
order 16 represents the nontrivial coset
(`TauCeti.SU2.mem_binaryOctahedralSubgroup_iff_mem_or_mul_inv_mem`), embeds
`TauCeti.SU2.binaryDihedralSubgroup 4` as a Sylow 2-subgroup, and generates the whole binary
octahedral subgroup together with `ω = (-1 + i + j + k) / 2`
(`TauCeti.SU2.binaryOctahedralSubgroup_eq_closure`), realizing the polyhedral `(2, 3, 4)` relations
`r ^ 4 = -1`, `ω ^ 3 = 1`, and `(r * ω⁻¹) ^ 2 = -1` (hence `orderOf (r * ω⁻¹) = 4`). Finally, the
unit-quaternion Cayley–Hamilton identity shows that every element satisfies `g ^ 8 = 1` or
`g ^ 6 = 1`, hence has order at most 8, distinguishing the binary octahedral group up to
isomorphism from cyclic groups of order 48 and from every dicyclic group `QuaternionGroup n`.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.SU2.binaryOctahedralCosetCoords`: the 24 `√2`-scaled integer coordinate vectors of the
  nontrivial coset.
* `TauCeti.SU2.binaryOctahedralSubgroup`: the binary octahedral subgroup of `SU(2)`.
* `TauCeti.SU2.binaryOctahedralCoordsEquiv`: its parametrization by
  `binaryTetrahedralCoords ⊕ binaryOctahedralCosetCoords`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.SU2.mem_binaryOctahedralSubgroup_iff_coords`,
  `TauCeti.SU2.mem_binaryOctahedralSubgroup_iff_exists_int`, and
  `TauCeti.SU2.mem_binaryOctahedralSubgroup_iff_mem_or_mul_inv_mem`: coordinate and coset
  characterizations of the binary octahedral subgroup.
* `TauCeti.SU2.natCard_binaryOctahedralSubgroup`: it has 48 elements.
* `TauCeti.SU2.relIndex_binaryTetrahedralSubgroup_binaryOctahedralSubgroup`: the binary tetrahedral
  subgroup has index 2 inside it (and is therefore normal).
* `TauCeti.SU2.binaryDihedralSubgroup_four_le_binaryOctahedralSubgroup`: it contains the binary
  dihedral subgroup of order 16.
* `TauCeti.SU2.binaryOctahedralSubgroup_eq_closure`: it is generated by `binaryDihedralRotation 4`
  and `binaryTetrahedralOmega`.
* `TauCeti.SU2.orderOf_le_eight_of_mem_binaryOctahedralSubgroup`,
  `TauCeti.SU2.not_isCyclic_binaryOctahedralSubgroup`, and
  `TauCeti.SU2.isEmpty_mulEquiv_quaternionGroup`: element-order bound and non-isomorphism with
  cyclic groups and with `QuaternionGroup n`.

## References

* J. H. Conway and D. A. Smith, *On Quaternions and Octonions*, A K Peters, 2003, Chapters 3 and 5,
  and §6.5.
* J.-H. Choi and J.-Y. Lee, *Binary Icosahedral Group and 600-Cell*, Symmetry 10 (2018), 326, §2.1.
-/

public section

namespace TauCeti.SU2

open Quaternion
open scoped Real

/-! ### The `√2`-scaled coset coordinates -/

/-- The `√2`-scaled coordinates `√2 q = (v₀, v₁, v₂, v₃)` of the 24 points `q` in the nontrivial
coset of the binary tetrahedral group inside the binary octahedral group: the integer vectors in
`{-1, 0, 1}⁴` with exactly two nonzero coordinates. -/
def binaryOctahedralCosetCoords : Finset (Fin 4 → ℤ) :=
  (Fintype.piFinset fun _ : Fin 4 => ({1, -1, 0} : Finset ℤ)).filter fun v =>
    (Finset.univ.filter fun i => v i ≠ 0).card = 2

/-- **The 24 `√2`-scaled coset coordinate vectors are distinct.** -/
@[simp]
theorem card_binaryOctahedralCosetCoords : binaryOctahedralCosetCoords.card = 24 := by
  decide

/-- Membership in `TauCeti.SU2.binaryOctahedralCosetCoords` in terms of support size and signs:
a vector has exactly two nonzero entries, and every nonzero entry is `1` or `-1`. -/
theorem mem_binaryOctahedralCosetCoords_iff_card {v : Fin 4 → ℤ} :
    v ∈ binaryOctahedralCosetCoords ↔
      (Finset.univ.filter fun i => v i ≠ 0).card = 2 ∧
        ∀ i, v i ≠ 0 → v i = 1 ∨ v i = -1 := by
  simp only [binaryOctahedralCosetCoords, Finset.mem_filter, Fintype.mem_piFinset,
    Finset.mem_insert, Finset.mem_singleton]
  refine ⟨fun ⟨hv, hcard⟩ => ⟨hcard, fun i hi => ?_⟩, fun ⟨hcard, hv⟩ => ⟨fun i => ?_, hcard⟩⟩
  · rcases hv i with h | h | h
    · exact .inl h
    · exact .inr h
    · exact absurd h hi
  · by_cases hi : v i = 0
    · exact .inr (.inr hi)
    · rcases hv i hi with h | h
      · exact .inl h
      · exact .inr (.inl h)

/-- **The `√2`-scaled coset vectors are the integer solutions of `v₀² + v₁² + v₂² + v₃² = 2`.** -/
theorem mem_binaryOctahedralCosetCoords_iff {v : Fin 4 → ℤ} :
    v ∈ binaryOctahedralCosetCoords ↔ ∑ i, v i ^ 2 = 2 := by
  refine ⟨fun hv => (by decide : ∀ v ∈ binaryOctahedralCosetCoords, ∑ i, v i ^ 2 = 2) v hv,
    fun hv => ?_⟩
  -- Each coordinate satisfies `v i ^ 2 ≤ 2`, hence lies in `[-1, 1]`.
  have hb (i : Fin 4) : v i ∈ Finset.Icc (-1 : ℤ) 1 := by
    have hi : v i ^ 2 ≤ 2 := by
      rw [← hv]
      exact Finset.single_le_sum (fun j _ => sq_nonneg (v j)) (Finset.mem_univ i)
    refine Finset.mem_Icc.mpr ⟨by_contra fun h => ?_, by_contra fun h => ?_⟩
    · have : v i ≤ -2 := by omega
      nlinarith
    · have : 2 ≤ v i := by omega
      nlinarith
  have key : ∀ a ∈ Finset.Icc (-1 : ℤ) 1, ∀ b ∈ Finset.Icc (-1 : ℤ) 1,
      ∀ c ∈ Finset.Icc (-1 : ℤ) 1, ∀ d ∈ Finset.Icc (-1 : ℤ) 1,
        a ^ 2 + b ^ 2 + c ^ 2 + d ^ 2 = 2 → ![a, b, c, d] ∈ binaryOctahedralCosetCoords := by
    decide
  have hv' := key _ (hb 0) _ (hb 1) _ (hb 2) _ (hb 3) (by simpa [Fin.sum_univ_four] using hv)
  convert hv' using 1
  ext i
  fin_cases i <;> simp

private theorem mem_Icc_of_mem_binaryTetrahedralCoords {v : Fin 4 → ℤ}
    (hv : v ∈ binaryTetrahedralCoords) (i : Fin 4) : v i ∈ Finset.Icc (-2 : ℤ) 2 := by
  have hsum := mem_binaryTetrahedralCoords_iff.mp hv
  have hi : v i ^ 2 ≤ 4 := by
    rw [← hsum]
    exact Finset.single_le_sum (fun j _ => sq_nonneg (v j)) (Finset.mem_univ i)
  refine Finset.mem_Icc.mpr ⟨by_contra fun h => ?_, by_contra fun h => ?_⟩
  · have : v i ≤ -3 := by omega
    nlinarith
  · have : 3 ≤ v i := by omega
    nlinarith

private theorem even_iff_even_of_mem_binaryTetrahedralCoords' {v : Fin 4 → ℤ}
    (hv : v ∈ binaryTetrahedralCoords) (i : Fin 4) : Even (v i) ↔ Even (v 0) := by
  have hsum : v 0 ^ 2 + v 1 ^ 2 + v 2 ^ 2 + v 3 ^ 2 = 4 := by
    simpa [Fin.sum_univ_four] using mem_binaryTetrahedralCoords_iff.mp hv
  have key : ∀ a ∈ Finset.Icc (-2 : ℤ) 2, ∀ b ∈ Finset.Icc (-2 : ℤ) 2,
      ∀ c ∈ Finset.Icc (-2 : ℤ) 2, ∀ d ∈ Finset.Icc (-2 : ℤ) 2,
        a ^ 2 + b ^ 2 + c ^ 2 + d ^ 2 = 4 →
          (Even b ↔ Even a) ∧ (Even c ↔ Even a) ∧ (Even d ↔ Even a) := by
    decide
  have h := key _ (mem_Icc_of_mem_binaryTetrahedralCoords hv 0)
    _ (mem_Icc_of_mem_binaryTetrahedralCoords hv 1)
    _ (mem_Icc_of_mem_binaryTetrahedralCoords hv 2)
    _ (mem_Icc_of_mem_binaryTetrahedralCoords hv 3) hsum
  fin_cases i
  exacts [Iff.rfl, h.1, h.2.1, h.2.2]

private theorem even_sum_of_mem_binaryOctahedralCosetCoords {v : Fin 4 → ℤ}
    (hv : v ∈ binaryOctahedralCosetCoords) : Even (v 0 + v 1 + v 2 + v 3) :=
  (by decide : ∀ v ∈ binaryOctahedralCosetCoords, Even (v 0 + v 1 + v 2 + v 3)) v hv

private theorem neg_coords_mem_binaryTetrahedralCoords {v : Fin 4 → ℤ}
    (hv : v ∈ binaryTetrahedralCoords) :
    ![v 0, -v 1, -v 2, -v 3] ∈ binaryTetrahedralCoords := by
  rw [mem_binaryTetrahedralCoords_iff, Fin.sum_univ_four] at hv ⊢
  simpa using hv

private theorem neg_coords_mem_binaryOctahedralCosetCoords {v : Fin 4 → ℤ}
    (hv : v ∈ binaryOctahedralCosetCoords) :
    ![v 0, -v 1, -v 2, -v 3] ∈ binaryOctahedralCosetCoords := by
  rw [mem_binaryOctahedralCosetCoords_iff, Fin.sum_univ_four] at hv ⊢
  simpa using hv

/-! ### Quaternions with `(1 / √2)`-scaled integer coordinates -/

private theorem normSq_mk_div_sqrt_two (a b c d : ℝ) :
    normSq (⟨a / √2, b / √2, c / √2, d / √2⟩ : ℍ[ℝ]) =
      (a ^ 2 + b ^ 2 + c ^ 2 + d ^ 2) / 2 := by
  simp only [normSq_def', div_pow, Real.sq_sqrt zero_le_two, add_div]

/-- An element of `SU(2)` with `(1 / √2)`-scaled integer quaternion coordinates has scaled
coordinates in `binaryOctahedralCosetCoords`, since its quaternion has norm one. -/
private theorem exists_mem_binaryOctahedralCosetCoords_of_coe_eq {g : SU2} {v : Fin 4 → ℤ}
    (hg : (g : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) =
      toComplexMatrix ⟨v 0 / √2, v 1 / √2, v 2 / √2, v 3 / √2⟩) :
    ∃ v ∈ binaryOctahedralCosetCoords,
      (g : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) =
        toComplexMatrix ⟨v 0 / √2, v 1 / √2, v 2 / √2, v 3 / √2⟩ := by
  have hdet := (Matrix.mem_specialUnitaryGroup_iff.mp g.2).2
  rw [hg, det_toComplexMatrix, normSq_mk_div_sqrt_two, ← Complex.ofReal_one, Complex.ofReal_inj,
    div_eq_one_iff_eq two_ne_zero] at hdet
  refine ⟨v, mem_binaryOctahedralCosetCoords_iff.mpr ?_, hg⟩
  rw [Fin.sum_univ_four]
  exact_mod_cast hdet

/-- Every vector in `binaryOctahedralCosetCoords` gives a unit quaternion, hence a matrix in
`SU(2)`. -/
private theorem toComplexMatrix_mem_of_mem_binaryOctahedralCosetCoords {v : Fin 4 → ℤ}
    (hv : v ∈ binaryOctahedralCosetCoords) :
    toComplexMatrix ⟨v 0 / √2, v 1 / √2, v 2 / √2, v 3 / √2⟩ ∈
      Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup (Fin 2) ℂ := by
  refine mem_specialUnitaryGroup_toComplexMatrix ((mem_unitary_iff_normSq_eq_one _).mpr ?_)
  have hv' := mem_binaryOctahedralCosetCoords_iff.mp hv
  rw [Fin.sum_univ_four] at hv'
  rw [normSq_mk_div_sqrt_two, div_eq_one_iff_eq two_ne_zero]
  exact_mod_cast hv'

/-- Disjointness of the two pieces: a half-integer quaternion never coincides with a `(1 / √2)`
coset quaternion, by irrationality of `√2`. -/
private theorem toComplexMatrix_div_two_ne_div_sqrt_two (v : Fin 4 → ℤ) {w : Fin 4 → ℤ}
    (hw : w ∈ binaryOctahedralCosetCoords) :
    toComplexMatrix ⟨v 0 / 2, v 1 / 2, v 2 / 2, v 3 / 2⟩ ≠
      toComplexMatrix ⟨w 0 / √2, w 1 / √2, w 2 / √2, w 3 / √2⟩ := by
  intro h
  have hinj := toComplexMatrix_injective h
  simp only [QuaternionAlgebra.mk.injEq] at hinj
  obtain ⟨hcard, -⟩ := mem_binaryOctahedralCosetCoords_iff_card.mp hw
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := Finset.card_pos.mp (hcard ▸ zero_lt_two)
  have hwi : w i ≠ 0 := (Finset.mem_filter.mp hi).2
  have hcoord : (v i : ℝ) / 2 = (w i : ℝ) / √2 := by
    fin_cases i
    exacts [hinj.1, hinj.2.1, hinj.2.2.1, hinj.2.2.2]
  have hsqrt : (0 : ℝ) < √2 := Real.sqrt_pos.mpr zero_lt_two
  have hwr : (w i : ℝ) / √2 ≠ 0 := div_ne_zero (Int.cast_ne_zero.mpr hwi) hsqrt.ne'
  have hvr : (v i : ℝ) ≠ 0 := fun hv0 => hwr (by rw [← hcoord, hv0, zero_div])
  have hcross : (v i : ℝ) * √2 = 2 * (w i : ℝ) := by
    have := (div_eq_div_iff (two_ne_zero' ℝ) hsqrt.ne').mp hcoord
    linarith
  refine irrational_sqrt_two ⟨(2 * w i : ℚ) / v i, ?_⟩
  push_cast
  rw [div_eq_iff hvr]
  linarith

/-- Multiplying a Hurwitz unit by a `(1 / √2)` coset quaternion produces another `(1 / √2)`-scaled
integer quaternion. -/
private theorem exists_mul_div_two_div_sqrt_two {v w : Fin 4 → ℤ}
    (hv : v ∈ binaryTetrahedralCoords) (hw : w ∈ binaryOctahedralCosetCoords) :
    ∃ u : Fin 4 → ℤ, (⟨v 0 / 2, v 1 / 2, v 2 / 2, v 3 / 2⟩ : ℍ[ℝ]) *
      ⟨w 0 / √2, w 1 / √2, w 2 / √2, w 3 / √2⟩ =
        ⟨u 0 / √2, u 1 / √2, u 2 / √2, u 3 / √2⟩ := by
  set x : ℍ[ℤ] := ⟨v 0, v 1, v 2, v 3⟩ * ⟨w 0, w 1, w 2, w 3⟩ with hx
  have hpv := even_iff_even_of_mem_binaryTetrahedralCoords' hv
  have hsw := even_sum_of_mem_binaryOctahedralCosetCoords hw
  have heven : Even x.re ∧ Even x.imI ∧ Even x.imJ ∧ Even x.imK := by
    by_cases hv0 : Even (v 0)
    · have hv1 : Even (v 1) := (hpv 1).mpr hv0
      have hv2 : Even (v 2) := (hpv 2).mpr hv0
      have hv3 : Even (v 3) := (hpv 3).mpr hv0
      simp [hx, Int.even_add, Int.even_sub, hv0, hv1, hv2, hv3]
    · have hv1 : ¬ Even (v 1) := mt (hpv 1).mp hv0
      have hv2 : ¬ Even (v 2) := mt (hpv 2).mp hv0
      have hv3 : ¬ Even (v 3) := mt (hpv 3).mp hv0
      simp only [Int.even_add] at hsw
      simp only [hx, re_mul, imI_mul, imJ_mul, imK_mul, Int.even_add, Int.even_sub, Int.even_mul,
        hv0, hv1, hv2, hv3, false_or]
      tauto
  obtain ⟨⟨a, ha⟩, ⟨b, hb⟩, ⟨c, hc⟩, ⟨d, hd⟩⟩ := heven
  simp only [hx, re_mul, imI_mul, imJ_mul, imK_mul] at ha hb hc hd
  rify at ha hb hc hd
  refine ⟨![a, b, c, d], ?_⟩
  have h2 : (√2 : ℝ) ≠ 0 := (Real.sqrt_pos.mpr zero_lt_two).ne'
  ext <;> simp only [re_mul, imI_mul, imJ_mul, imK_mul, Matrix.cons_val, div_mul_div_comm] <;>
    field_simp
  · linarith [ha]
  · linarith [hb]
  · linarith [hc]
  · linarith [hd]

/-- Multiplying a `(1 / √2)` coset quaternion by a Hurwitz unit produces another `(1 / √2)`-scaled
integer quaternion, deduced from `exists_mul_div_two_div_sqrt_two` by quaternion conjugation. -/
private theorem exists_mul_div_sqrt_two_div_two {v w : Fin 4 → ℤ}
    (hv : v ∈ binaryOctahedralCosetCoords) (hw : w ∈ binaryTetrahedralCoords) :
    ∃ u : Fin 4 → ℤ, (⟨v 0 / √2, v 1 / √2, v 2 / √2, v 3 / √2⟩ : ℍ[ℝ]) *
      ⟨w 0 / 2, w 1 / 2, w 2 / 2, w 3 / 2⟩ =
        ⟨u 0 / √2, u 1 / √2, u 2 / √2, u 3 / √2⟩ := by
  obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := exists_mul_div_two_div_sqrt_two
    (neg_coords_mem_binaryTetrahedralCoords hw) (neg_coords_mem_binaryOctahedralCosetCoords hv)
  refine ⟨![u 0, -u 1, -u 2, -u 3], ?_⟩
  have hstar := congrArg star hu
  rw [star_mul] at hstar
  convert hstar using 1
  · ext <;> simp [neg_div]
  · ext <;> simp [neg_div]

/-- Multiplying two `(1 / √2)`-scaled integer quaternions yields a half-integer quaternion. -/
private theorem exists_mul_div_sqrt_two_div_sqrt_two (v w : Fin 4 → ℤ) :
    ∃ u : Fin 4 → ℤ, (⟨v 0 / √2, v 1 / √2, v 2 / √2, v 3 / √2⟩ : ℍ[ℝ]) *
      ⟨w 0 / √2, w 1 / √2, w 2 / √2, w 3 / √2⟩ =
        ⟨u 0 / 2, u 1 / 2, u 2 / 2, u 3 / 2⟩ := by
  set x : ℍ[ℤ] := ⟨v 0, v 1, v 2, v 3⟩ * ⟨w 0, w 1, w 2, w 3⟩ with hx
  refine ⟨![x.re, x.imI, x.imJ, x.imK], ?_⟩
  ext <;> simp only [hx, re_mul, imI_mul, imJ_mul, imK_mul, Matrix.cons_val, div_mul_div_comm,
    Real.mul_self_sqrt zero_le_two, Int.cast_sub, Int.cast_add, Int.cast_mul, sub_div, add_div]

/-! ### The binary octahedral subgroup -/

/-- **The binary octahedral subgroup of `SU(2)`**: the 48 matrices obtained by adjoining to the 24
elements of `TauCeti.SU2.binaryTetrahedralSubgroup` the 24 matrices of the unit quaternions
`(v₀ + v₁ i + v₂ j + v₃ k) / √2` for `v` in `TauCeti.SU2.binaryOctahedralCosetCoords`. -/
noncomputable def binaryOctahedralSubgroup : Subgroup SU2 where
  carrier := {g | g ∈ binaryTetrahedralSubgroup ∨ ∃ v ∈ binaryOctahedralCosetCoords,
    (g : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) =
      toComplexMatrix ⟨v 0 / √2, v 1 / √2, v 2 / √2, v 3 / √2⟩}
  mul_mem' := by
    rintro g h (hg | ⟨v, hv, hg⟩) (hh | ⟨w, hw, hh⟩)
    · exact .inl (binaryTetrahedralSubgroup.mul_mem hg hh)
    · obtain ⟨v, hv, hg⟩ := mem_binaryTetrahedralSubgroup_iff.mp hg
      obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := exists_mul_div_two_div_sqrt_two hv hw
      refine .inr (exists_mem_binaryOctahedralCosetCoords_of_coe_eq (v := u) ?_)
      rw [← hu, map_mul, ← hg, ← hh, Submonoid.coe_mul]
    · obtain ⟨w, hw, hh⟩ := mem_binaryTetrahedralSubgroup_iff.mp hh
      obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := exists_mul_div_sqrt_two_div_two hv hw
      refine .inr (exists_mem_binaryOctahedralCosetCoords_of_coe_eq (v := u) ?_)
      rw [← hu, map_mul, ← hg, ← hh, Submonoid.coe_mul]
    · obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := exists_mul_div_sqrt_two_div_sqrt_two v w
      refine .inl (mem_binaryTetrahedralSubgroup_iff_exists_int.mpr ⟨u, ?_⟩)
      rw [← hu, map_mul, ← hg, ← hh, Submonoid.coe_mul]
  one_mem' := .inl binaryTetrahedralSubgroup.one_mem
  inv_mem' := by
    rintro g (hg | ⟨v, -, hg⟩)
    · exact .inl (binaryTetrahedralSubgroup.inv_mem hg)
    · refine .inr (exists_mem_binaryOctahedralCosetCoords_of_coe_eq
        (v := ![v 0, -v 1, -v 2, -v 3]) ?_)
      rw [← Matrix.star_eq_inv, Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup.coe_star, hg, ← map_star]
      congr 1
      ext <;> simp [neg_div]

/-- Membership in `TauCeti.SU2.binaryOctahedralSubgroup`: either membership in the binary
tetrahedral subgroup or a `√2`-scaled coordinate vector in `binaryOctahedralCosetCoords`. -/
theorem mem_binaryOctahedralSubgroup_iff {g : SU2} :
    g ∈ binaryOctahedralSubgroup ↔
      g ∈ binaryTetrahedralSubgroup ∨ ∃ v ∈ binaryOctahedralCosetCoords,
        (g : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) =
          toComplexMatrix ⟨v 0 / √2, v 1 / √2, v 2 / √2, v 3 / √2⟩ :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- **The binary octahedral subgroup consists of the unit quaternions with coordinates in
`(1 / 2) ℤ⁴` or `(1 / √2) ℤ⁴`.** -/
theorem mem_binaryOctahedralSubgroup_iff_exists_int {g : SU2} :
    g ∈ binaryOctahedralSubgroup ↔
      (∃ v : Fin 4 → ℤ,
        (g : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) =
          toComplexMatrix ⟨v 0 / 2, v 1 / 2, v 2 / 2, v 3 / 2⟩) ∨
      (∃ v : Fin 4 → ℤ,
        (g : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) =
          toComplexMatrix ⟨v 0 / √2, v 1 / √2, v 2 / √2, v 3 / √2⟩) := by
  rw [mem_binaryOctahedralSubgroup_iff, mem_binaryTetrahedralSubgroup_iff_exists_int]
  exact or_congr_right ⟨fun ⟨v, _, hg⟩ => ⟨v, hg⟩,
    fun ⟨_, hg⟩ => exists_mem_binaryOctahedralCosetCoords_of_coe_eq hg⟩

/-- **Coordinate characterization of the binary octahedral subgroup**: it is obtained from the
binary tetrahedral subgroup by adjoining the 24 unit quaternions with exactly two nonzero
coordinates, both equal to `±1 / √2`. -/
theorem mem_binaryOctahedralSubgroup_iff_coords {g : SU2} :
    g ∈ binaryOctahedralSubgroup ↔
      g ∈ binaryTetrahedralSubgroup ∨
        ∃ c : Fin 4 → ℝ,
          (Finset.univ.filter fun i => c i ≠ 0).card = 2 ∧
          (∀ i, c i ≠ 0 → c i = 1 / √2 ∨ c i = -(1 / √2)) ∧
          (g : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) = toComplexMatrix ⟨c 0, c 1, c 2, c 3⟩ := by
  have hsqrt : (0 : ℝ) < √2 := Real.sqrt_pos.mpr zero_lt_two
  refine or_congr_right ⟨fun ⟨v, hv, hg⟩ => ?_, fun ⟨c, hcard, hsign, hg⟩ => ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨hcard, hsign⟩ := mem_binaryOctahedralCosetCoords_iff_card.mp hv
    refine ⟨fun i => (v i : ℝ) / √2, ?_, fun i hi => ?_, hg⟩
    · convert hcard using 2
      ext i
      simp [hsqrt.ne']
    · have hvi : v i ≠ 0 := fun h0 => hi (by simp [h0])
      rcases hsign i hvi with h | h <;> simp [h, neg_div]
  · classical
    let v : Fin 4 → ℤ := fun i => if c i = 0 then 0 else if c i = 1 / √2 then 1 else -1
    have hvc (i : Fin 4) : (v i : ℝ) / √2 = c i := by
      by_cases h0 : c i = 0
      · simp only [v, ite_eq_left h0, Int.cast_zero, zero_div, h0]
      · rcases hsign i h0 with h | h
        · simp only [v, ite_eq_right h0, h, ite_true, Int.cast_one]
        · have hne : -(1 / √2) ≠ 1 / √2 := by
            have : (0 : ℝ) < 1 / √2 := div_pos zero_lt_one hsqrt
            linarith
          simp only [v, ite_eq_right h0, h, ite_eq_right hne, Int.cast_neg, Int.cast_one, neg_div]
    have hvnz (i : Fin 4) : v i ≠ 0 ↔ c i ≠ 0 :=
      ⟨fun hvi hc0 => hvi (by simp only [v, ite_eq_left hc0]),
        fun hci hv0 => hci (by rw [← hvc i, hv0, Int.cast_zero, zero_div])⟩
    refine ⟨v, mem_binaryOctahedralCosetCoords_iff_card.mpr ⟨?_, fun i hi => ?_⟩, ?_⟩
    · rw [← hcard]
      congr 1
      ext i
      simp only [Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_univ, true_and, hvnz i]
    · have h0 : c i ≠ 0 := (hvnz i).mp hi
      by_cases h1 : c i = 1 / √2
      · exact .inl (by simp only [v, ite_eq_right h0, ite_eq_left h1])
      · exact .inr (by simp only [v, ite_eq_right h0, ite_eq_right h1])
    · simp only [hvc, hg]

/-! ### Parametrization and cardinality -/

/-- Map sending the two coordinate sets `binaryTetrahedralCoords` and
`binaryOctahedralCosetCoords` to the binary octahedral subgroup. -/
private noncomputable def binaryOctahedralCoordsFun :
    binaryTetrahedralCoords ⊕ binaryOctahedralCosetCoords → binaryOctahedralSubgroup
  | .inl v => ⟨(binaryTetrahedralCoordsEquiv v : SU2), .inl (binaryTetrahedralCoordsEquiv v).2⟩
  | .inr v => ⟨⟨_, toComplexMatrix_mem_of_mem_binaryOctahedralCosetCoords v.2⟩,
      .inr ⟨v, v.2, rfl⟩⟩

private theorem binaryOctahedralCoordsFun_bijective :
    Function.Bijective binaryOctahedralCoordsFun := by
  refine ⟨fun x y hxy => ?_, fun g => ?_⟩
  · have hmat := congrArg (fun z : binaryOctahedralSubgroup =>
      ((z : SU2) : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ)) hxy
    dsimp only [binaryOctahedralCoordsFun] at hmat
    cases x with
    | inl v =>
      cases y with
      | inl w =>
        exact congrArg Sum.inl
          (binaryTetrahedralCoordsEquiv.injective (Subtype.ext (Subtype.ext hmat)))
      | inr w =>
        rw [coe_binaryTetrahedralCoordsEquiv_apply] at hmat
        exact absurd hmat (toComplexMatrix_div_two_ne_div_sqrt_two v w.2)
    | inr v =>
      cases y with
      | inl w =>
        rw [coe_binaryTetrahedralCoordsEquiv_apply] at hmat
        exact absurd hmat.symm (toComplexMatrix_div_two_ne_div_sqrt_two w v.2)
      | inr w =>
        have hq := toComplexMatrix_injective hmat
        have hsqrt : (√2 : ℝ) ≠ 0 := (Real.sqrt_pos.mpr zero_lt_two).ne'
        simp only [QuaternionAlgebra.mk.injEq, div_left_inj₀ hsqrt, Int.cast_inj] at hq
        obtain ⟨h0, h1, h2, h3⟩ := hq
        congr 1
        ext i
        fin_cases i
        exacts [h0, h1, h2, h3]
  · rcases g.2 with hg | ⟨v, hv, hg⟩
    · refine ⟨.inl (binaryTetrahedralCoordsEquiv.symm ⟨g.1, hg⟩), Subtype.ext ?_⟩
      simp [binaryOctahedralCoordsFun]
    · exact ⟨.inr ⟨v, hv⟩, Subtype.ext (Subtype.ext hg.symm)⟩

/-- **The 48 coordinate vectors parametrize the binary octahedral subgroup**: the 24 doubled
tetrahedral vectors `v` give `(v₀ + v₁ i + v₂ j + v₃ k) / 2` and the 24 coset vectors `w` give
`(w₀ + w₁ i + w₂ j + w₃ k) / √2`. -/
noncomputable def binaryOctahedralCoordsEquiv :
    binaryTetrahedralCoords ⊕ binaryOctahedralCosetCoords ≃ binaryOctahedralSubgroup :=
  Equiv.ofBijective _ binaryOctahedralCoordsFun_bijective

@[simp]
theorem coe_binaryOctahedralCoordsEquiv_inl (v : binaryTetrahedralCoords) :
    ((binaryOctahedralCoordsEquiv (.inl v) : SU2) : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) =
      toComplexMatrix ⟨(v : Fin 4 → ℤ) 0 / 2, (v : Fin 4 → ℤ) 1 / 2, (v : Fin 4 → ℤ) 2 / 2,
        (v : Fin 4 → ℤ) 3 / 2⟩ :=
  coe_binaryTetrahedralCoordsEquiv_apply v

@[simp]
theorem coe_binaryOctahedralCoordsEquiv_inr (v : binaryOctahedralCosetCoords) :
    ((binaryOctahedralCoordsEquiv (.inr v) : SU2) : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) =
      toComplexMatrix ⟨(v : Fin 4 → ℤ) 0 / √2, (v : Fin 4 → ℤ) 1 / √2,
        (v : Fin 4 → ℤ) 2 / √2, (v : Fin 4 → ℤ) 3 / √2⟩ := (rfl)

instance : Finite binaryOctahedralSubgroup :=
  Finite.of_equiv _ binaryOctahedralCoordsEquiv

/-- **The binary octahedral subgroup has 48 elements.** -/
@[simp]
theorem natCard_binaryOctahedralSubgroup : Nat.card binaryOctahedralSubgroup = 48 := by
  rw [← Nat.card_congr binaryOctahedralCoordsEquiv, Nat.card_eq_fintype_card, Fintype.card_sum,
    Fintype.card_coe, Fintype.card_coe, card_binaryTetrahedralCoords,
    card_binaryOctahedralCosetCoords]

/-! ### Subgroups and generators -/

/-- **The binary tetrahedral subgroup is contained in the binary octahedral subgroup.** -/
theorem binaryTetrahedralSubgroup_le_binaryOctahedralSubgroup :
    binaryTetrahedralSubgroup ≤ binaryOctahedralSubgroup :=
  fun _ hg => .inl hg

/-- **The binary tetrahedral subgroup has relative index 2 in the binary octahedral subgroup.** -/
@[simp]
theorem relIndex_binaryTetrahedralSubgroup_binaryOctahedralSubgroup :
    binaryTetrahedralSubgroup.relIndex binaryOctahedralSubgroup = 2 := by
  have h := binaryTetrahedralSubgroup.relIndex_mul_card binaryOctahedralSubgroup
  rw [inf_of_le_left binaryTetrahedralSubgroup_le_binaryOctahedralSubgroup,
    natCard_binaryTetrahedralSubgroup, natCard_binaryOctahedralSubgroup] at h
  omega

/-- The binary tetrahedral subgroup is a normal subgroup of the binary octahedral subgroup, since
it has index 2. -/
instance : (binaryTetrahedralSubgroup.subgroupOf binaryOctahedralSubgroup).Normal :=
  Subgroup.normal_of_index_eq_two relIndex_binaryTetrahedralSubgroup_binaryOctahedralSubgroup

/-- The eighth-turn generator `binaryDihedralRotation 4` of the binary dihedral group of order 16
is the matrix of the quaternion `(1 + i) / √2`. -/
theorem coe_binaryDihedralRotation_four_eq_toComplexMatrix :
    (binaryDihedralRotation 4 : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) =
      toComplexMatrix ⟨1 / √2, 1 / √2, 0, 0⟩ := by
  have hhalf : √2 / 2 = 1 / √2 := by
    rw [div_eq_div_iff two_ne_zero (Real.sqrt_pos.mpr zero_lt_two).ne', one_mul,
      Real.mul_self_sqrt zero_le_two]
  rw [coe_binaryDihedralRotation_eq_toComplexMatrix, Nat.cast_ofNat, Real.cos_pi_div_four,
    Real.sin_pi_div_four, hhalf]

@[simp]
theorem binaryDihedralRotation_four_mem_binaryOctahedralSubgroup :
    binaryDihedralRotation 4 ∈ binaryOctahedralSubgroup := by
  refine .inr ⟨![1, 1, 0, 0], by decide, ?_⟩
  rw [coe_binaryDihedralRotation_four_eq_toComplexMatrix]
  congr 1
  ext <;> simp

/-- The eighth-turn generator `binaryDihedralRotation 4` represents the nontrivial coset of the
binary tetrahedral subgroup. -/
theorem binaryDihedralRotation_four_notMem_binaryTetrahedralSubgroup :
    binaryDihedralRotation 4 ∉ binaryTetrahedralSubgroup := by
  intro h
  obtain ⟨v, -, hv⟩ := mem_binaryTetrahedralSubgroup_iff.mp h
  rw [coe_binaryDihedralRotation_four_eq_toComplexMatrix] at hv
  have hmat : toComplexMatrix ⟨v 0 / 2, v 1 / 2, v 2 / 2, v 3 / 2⟩ =
      toComplexMatrix ⟨(![1, 1, 0, 0] : Fin 4 → ℤ) 0 / √2, (![1, 1, 0, 0] : Fin 4 → ℤ) 1 / √2,
        (![1, 1, 0, 0] : Fin 4 → ℤ) 2 / √2, (![1, 1, 0, 0] : Fin 4 → ℤ) 3 / √2⟩ := by
    rw [← hv]
    congr 1
    ext <;> simp
  exact toComplexMatrix_div_two_ne_div_sqrt_two v (by decide) hmat

/-- **Coset decomposition over the binary tetrahedral subgroup**: an element of `SU(2)` lies in
the binary octahedral subgroup if and only if either it lies in `binaryTetrahedralSubgroup` or
`g * (binaryDihedralRotation 4)⁻¹` does. -/
theorem mem_binaryOctahedralSubgroup_iff_mem_or_mul_inv_mem {g : SU2} :
    g ∈ binaryOctahedralSubgroup ↔
      g ∈ binaryTetrahedralSubgroup ∨
        g * (binaryDihedralRotation 4)⁻¹ ∈ binaryTetrahedralSubgroup := by
  constructor
  · rintro (hg | ⟨v, -, hg⟩)
    · exact .inl hg
    · obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := exists_mul_div_sqrt_two_div_sqrt_two v ![1, -1, 0, 0]
      refine .inr (mem_binaryTetrahedralSubgroup_iff_exists_int.mpr ⟨u, ?_⟩)
      have hr : (((binaryDihedralRotation 4)⁻¹ : SU2) : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) =
          toComplexMatrix ⟨(![1, -1, 0, 0] : Fin 4 → ℤ) 0 / √2,
            (![1, -1, 0, 0] : Fin 4 → ℤ) 1 / √2,
            (![1, -1, 0, 0] : Fin 4 → ℤ) 2 / √2,
            (![1, -1, 0, 0] : Fin 4 → ℤ) 3 / √2⟩ := by
        rw [← Matrix.star_eq_inv, Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup.coe_star,
          coe_binaryDihedralRotation_four_eq_toComplexMatrix, ← map_star]
        congr 1
        ext <;> simp [neg_div]
      rw [← hu, map_mul, ← hg, ← hr, Submonoid.coe_mul]
  · rintro (hg | hg)
    · exact binaryTetrahedralSubgroup_le_binaryOctahedralSubgroup hg
    · simpa only [inv_mul_cancel_right] using
        binaryOctahedralSubgroup.mul_mem (binaryTetrahedralSubgroup_le_binaryOctahedralSubgroup hg)
          binaryDihedralRotation_four_mem_binaryOctahedralSubgroup

/-- **The binary octahedral subgroup contains the binary dihedral subgroup of order 16** as a
Sylow 2-subgroup. -/
theorem binaryDihedralSubgroup_four_le_binaryOctahedralSubgroup :
    binaryDihedralSubgroup 4 ≤ binaryOctahedralSubgroup := by
  rw [binaryDihedralSubgroup_eq_closure, Subgroup.closure_le, Set.insert_subset_iff,
    Set.singleton_subset_iff]
  exact ⟨binaryDihedralRotation_four_mem_binaryOctahedralSubgroup,
    binaryTetrahedralSubgroup_le_binaryOctahedralSubgroup
      (binaryDihedralSubgroup_two_le_binaryTetrahedralSubgroup
        (inv_mem (weylElement_mem_binaryDihedralSubgroup 2)))⟩

@[simp]
theorem binaryTetrahedralOmega_mem_binaryOctahedralSubgroup :
    binaryTetrahedralOmega ∈ binaryOctahedralSubgroup :=
  binaryTetrahedralSubgroup_le_binaryOctahedralSubgroup
    binaryTetrahedralOmega_mem_binaryTetrahedralSubgroup

/-- The square of `binaryDihedralRotation 4` (`(1 + i) / √2`) is
`binaryDihedralRotation 2` (`i`). -/
theorem binaryDihedralRotation_four_sq :
    binaryDihedralRotation 4 ^ 2 = binaryDihedralRotation 2 := by
  apply Subtype.ext
  rw [SubmonoidClass.coe_pow, coe_binaryDihedralRotation_four_eq_toComplexMatrix, ← map_pow,
    coe_binaryDihedralRotation_eq_toComplexMatrix]
  congr 1
  ext <;> simp only [sq, re_mul, imI_mul, imJ_mul, imK_mul, div_mul_div_comm,
    Real.mul_self_sqrt zero_le_two, Nat.cast_ofNat, Real.cos_pi_div_two, Real.sin_pi_div_two] <;>
    norm_num

/-- In the polyhedral `(2, 3, 4)` presentation, `r * ω⁻¹ = (-i - k) / √2` squares to `-1`. -/
theorem coe_binaryDihedralRotation_four_mul_binaryTetrahedralOmega_inv_sq :
    (((binaryDihedralRotation 4 * binaryTetrahedralOmega⁻¹) ^ 2 : SU2) :
      Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) = -1 := by
  have hinv : ((binaryTetrahedralOmega⁻¹ : SU2) : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) =
      toComplexMatrix ⟨-1 / 2, -1 / 2, -1 / 2, -1 / 2⟩ := by
    rw [← Matrix.star_eq_inv, Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup.coe_star, coe_binaryTetrahedralOmega,
      ← map_star]
    congr 1
    ext <;> simp [neg_div]
  have hmul : (⟨1 / √2, 1 / √2, 0, 0⟩ : ℍ[ℝ]) * ⟨-1 / 2, -1 / 2, -1 / 2, -1 / 2⟩ =
      ⟨0, -1 / √2, 0, -1 / √2⟩ := by
    ext <;> simp <;> ring
  rw [SubmonoidClass.coe_pow, Submonoid.coe_mul, coe_binaryDihedralRotation_four_eq_toComplexMatrix,
    hinv, ← map_mul, hmul, ← map_pow, ← map_one toComplexMatrix, ← map_neg]
  congr 1
  ext <;> simp only [sq, re_mul, imI_mul, imJ_mul, imK_mul, div_mul_div_comm,
    Real.mul_self_sqrt zero_le_two, re_neg, re_one, imI_neg, imI_one, imJ_neg, imJ_one, imK_neg,
    imK_one] <;> norm_num

/-- In the polyhedral `(2, 3, 4)` presentation, `r * ω⁻¹` has order `4` in `SU(2)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem orderOf_binaryDihedralRotation_four_mul_binaryTetrahedralOmega_inv :
    orderOf (binaryDihedralRotation 4 * binaryTetrahedralOmega⁻¹) = 4 := by
  change _ = 2 ^ 2
  have : Fact (Nat.Prime 2) := ⟨Nat.prime_two⟩
  refine orderOf_eq_prime_pow (fun h => ?_) ?_
  · rw [pow_one] at h
    have hmat : (((binaryDihedralRotation 4 * binaryTetrahedralOmega⁻¹) ^ 2 : SU2) :
        Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) = 1 := by
      rw [h, OneMemClass.coe_one]
    rw [coe_binaryDihedralRotation_four_mul_binaryTetrahedralOmega_inv_sq] at hmat
    have h00 := congrFun (congrFun hmat 0) 0
    norm_num at h00
  · apply Subtype.ext
    rw [show 2 ^ (1 + 1) = 2 * 2 from rfl, pow_mul, SubmonoidClass.coe_pow,
      coe_binaryDihedralRotation_four_mul_binaryTetrahedralOmega_inv_sq, neg_one_sq,
      OneMemClass.coe_one]

/-- The quarter-turn generator `weylElement⁻¹` (`j`) is expressed in terms of
`r = binaryDihedralRotation 4` and `ω = binaryTetrahedralOmega` by `r² * (r * ω)² = j`. -/
private theorem binaryDihedralRotation_four_sq_mul_mul_omega_sq :
    binaryDihedralRotation 4 ^ 2 * (binaryDihedralRotation 4 * binaryTetrahedralOmega) ^ 2 =
      weylElement⁻¹ := by
  have hrω : (⟨1 / √2, 1 / √2, 0, 0⟩ : ℍ[ℝ]) * ⟨-1 / 2, 1 / 2, 1 / 2, 1 / 2⟩ =
      ⟨-1 / √2, 0, 0, 1 / √2⟩ := by
    ext <;> simp <;> ring
  have hrω2 : (⟨-1 / √2, 0, 0, 1 / √2⟩ : ℍ[ℝ]) ^ 2 = ⟨0, 0, 0, -1⟩ := by
    ext <;> simp only [sq, re_mul, imI_mul, imJ_mul, imK_mul, div_mul_div_comm,
      Real.mul_self_sqrt zero_le_two] <;> norm_num
  apply Subtype.ext
  rw [binaryDihedralRotation_four_sq, Submonoid.coe_mul, SubmonoidClass.coe_pow, Submonoid.coe_mul,
    coe_binaryDihedralRotation_eq_toComplexMatrix,
    coe_binaryDihedralRotation_four_eq_toComplexMatrix, coe_binaryTetrahedralOmega,
    coe_weylElement_inv_eq_toComplexMatrix, ← map_mul, hrω, ← map_pow, hrω2, ← map_mul]
  congr 1
  ext <;> simp only [Nat.cast_ofNat, Real.cos_pi_div_two, Real.sin_pi_div_two] <;> norm_num

/-- **The binary octahedral subgroup is generated by `r = binaryDihedralRotation 4` and
`ω = binaryTetrahedralOmega`.** -/
theorem binaryOctahedralSubgroup_eq_closure :
    binaryOctahedralSubgroup =
      Subgroup.closure {binaryDihedralRotation 4, binaryTetrahedralOmega} := by
  set H := Subgroup.closure {binaryDihedralRotation 4, binaryTetrahedralOmega}
  have hr : binaryDihedralRotation 4 ∈ H := Subgroup.subset_closure (by simp)
  have hω : binaryTetrahedralOmega ∈ H := Subgroup.subset_closure (by simp)
  have hs : weylElement⁻¹ ∈ H := by
    rw [← binaryDihedralRotation_four_sq_mul_mul_omega_sq]
    exact mul_mem (pow_mem hr 2) (pow_mem (mul_mem hr hω) 2)
  have hle : H ≤ binaryOctahedralSubgroup := by
    rw [Subgroup.closure_le, Set.insert_subset_iff, Set.singleton_subset_iff]
    exact ⟨binaryDihedralRotation_four_mem_binaryOctahedralSubgroup,
      binaryTetrahedralOmega_mem_binaryOctahedralSubgroup⟩
  have : Finite H := Finite.of_injective _ (Subgroup.inclusion_injective hle)
  have h16 : 16 ∣ Nat.card H := by
    have hD : binaryDihedralSubgroup 4 ≤ H := by
      rw [binaryDihedralSubgroup_eq_closure, Subgroup.closure_le, Set.insert_subset_iff,
        Set.singleton_subset_iff]
      exact ⟨hr, hs⟩
    simpa using Subgroup.card_dvd_of_le hD
  have h3 : 3 ∣ Nat.card H := by
    simpa using H.orderOf_dvd_natCard hω
  refine (Subgroup.eq_of_le_of_card_ge hle ?_).symm
  rw [natCard_binaryOctahedralSubgroup]
  exact Nat.le_of_dvd Nat.card_pos (Nat.Coprime.mul_dvd_of_dvd_of_dvd (by norm_num) h16 h3)

/-! ### Element orders and exclusion of cyclic and dicyclic groups -/

/-- Cayley–Hamilton identity for unit quaternions: `q² = (2 Re q) q - 1`. -/
private theorem sq_eq_two_re_smul_sub_one {q : ℍ[ℝ]} (hq : normSq q = 1) :
    q ^ 2 = (2 * q.re) • q - 1 := by
  rw [normSq_def'] at hq
  ext <;> simp only [sq, re_mul, imI_mul, imJ_mul, imK_mul, QuaternionAlgebra.re_sub,
    QuaternionAlgebra.imI_sub, QuaternionAlgebra.imJ_sub, QuaternionAlgebra.imK_sub,
    QuaternionAlgebra.re_smul, QuaternionAlgebra.imI_smul, QuaternionAlgebra.imJ_smul,
    QuaternionAlgebra.imK_smul, re_one, imI_one, imJ_one, imK_one, smul_eq_mul]
  · linear_combination -hq
  all_goals ring

private theorem pow_three_of_normSq_eq_one {q : ℍ[ℝ]} (hq : normSq q = 1) :
    q ^ 3 = ((2 * q.re) ^ 2 - 1) • q - (2 * q.re) • (1 : ℍ[ℝ]) := by
  rw [pow_succ, sq_eq_two_re_smul_sub_one hq, sub_mul, smul_mul_assoc, one_mul, ← sq,
    sq_eq_two_re_smul_sub_one hq, smul_sub, smul_smul]
  ext <;> simp <;> ring

private theorem pow_four_of_normSq_eq_one {q : ℍ[ℝ]} (hq : normSq q = 1) :
    q ^ 4 = ((2 * q.re) * ((2 * q.re) ^ 2 - 2)) • q + (1 - (2 * q.re) ^ 2) • (1 : ℍ[ℝ]) := by
  rw [pow_succ, pow_three_of_normSq_eq_one hq, sub_mul, smul_mul_assoc, smul_mul_assoc, one_mul,
    ← sq, sq_eq_two_re_smul_sub_one hq, smul_sub, smul_smul]
  ext <;> simp <;> ring

private theorem pow_eight_or_pow_six_of_mem_binaryTetrahedralCoords {g : SU2} {v : Fin 4 → ℤ}
    (hv : v ∈ binaryTetrahedralCoords)
    (hvg : (g : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) = toComplexMatrix ⟨v 0 / 2, v 1 / 2, v 2 / 2, v 3 / 2⟩) :
    g ^ 8 = 1 ∨ g ^ 6 = 1 := by
  set q : ℍ[ℝ] := ⟨v 0 / 2, v 1 / 2, v 2 / 2, v 3 / 2⟩
  have hq : normSq q = 1 := by
    have hdet := (Matrix.mem_specialUnitaryGroup_iff.mp g.2).2
    rw [hvg, det_toComplexMatrix, ← Complex.ofReal_one, Complex.ofReal_inj] at hdet
    exact hdet
  have h2re : 2 * q.re = (v 0 : ℝ) := by simp only [q]; ring
  have hb0 := Finset.mem_Icc.mp (mem_Icc_of_mem_binaryTetrahedralCoords hv 0)
  have hv0 : v 0 ^ 2 = 4 ∨ v 0 = 0 ∨ v 0 ^ 2 = 1 := by
    rcases (by omega : v 0 = -2 ∨ v 0 = -1 ∨ v 0 = 0 ∨ v 0 = 1 ∨ v 0 = 2) with
      h | h | h | h | h <;> simp [h]
  rcases hv0 with hsq4 | h0 | hsq
  · left
    have hsum : v 0 ^ 2 + v 1 ^ 2 + v 2 ^ 2 + v 3 ^ 2 = 4 := by
      simpa [Fin.sum_univ_four] using mem_binaryTetrahedralCoords_iff.mp hv
    have hv1 : v 1 = 0 := by nlinarith [sq_nonneg (v 2), sq_nonneg (v 3)]
    have hv2 : v 2 = 0 := by nlinarith [sq_nonneg (v 1), sq_nonneg (v 3)]
    have hv3 : v 3 = 0 := by nlinarith [sq_nonneg (v 1), sq_nonneg (v 2)]
    have hsq4' : (v 0 : ℝ) ^ 2 = 4 := by exact_mod_cast hsq4
    have hq2 : q ^ 2 = 1 := by
      rw [sq]
      ext <;> simp only [q, hv1, hv2, hv3, Int.cast_zero, zero_div, re_mul, imI_mul, imJ_mul,
        imK_mul, re_one, imI_one, imJ_one, imK_one]
      · linear_combination hsq4' / 4
      all_goals norm_num
    have h8 : 8 = 2 * 4 := rfl
    apply Subtype.ext
    rw [SubmonoidClass.coe_pow, hvg, ← map_pow, h8, pow_mul, hq2, one_pow, map_one,
      OneMemClass.coe_one]
  · left
    have hq4 : q ^ 4 = 1 := by rw [pow_four_of_normSq_eq_one hq, h2re, h0]; ext <;> norm_num
    have h8 : 8 = 4 * 2 := rfl
    apply Subtype.ext
    rw [SubmonoidClass.coe_pow, hvg, ← map_pow, h8, pow_mul, hq4, one_pow, map_one,
      OneMemClass.coe_one]
  · right
    have hsq' : (v 0 : ℝ) ^ 2 = 1 := by exact_mod_cast hsq
    have hq6 : q ^ 6 = 1 := by
      have hq3 : q ^ 3 = -(v 0 : ℝ) • (1 : ℍ[ℝ]) := by
        rw [pow_three_of_normSq_eq_one hq, h2re, hsq']
        ext <;> simp
      have h6 : 6 = 3 * 2 := rfl
      rw [h6, pow_mul, hq3, sq, smul_mul_smul_comm, mul_one, ← sq, neg_sq, hsq', one_smul]
    apply Subtype.ext
    rw [SubmonoidClass.coe_pow, hvg, ← map_pow, hq6, map_one, OneMemClass.coe_one]

private theorem pow_eight_of_mem_binaryOctahedralCosetCoords {g : SU2} {v : Fin 4 → ℤ}
    (hv : v ∈ binaryOctahedralCosetCoords)
    (hvg : (g : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) =
      toComplexMatrix ⟨v 0 / √2, v 1 / √2, v 2 / √2, v 3 / √2⟩) :
    g ^ 8 = 1 := by
  set q : ℍ[ℝ] := ⟨v 0 / √2, v 1 / √2, v 2 / √2, v 3 / √2⟩
  have hq : normSq q = 1 := by
    have hdet := (Matrix.mem_specialUnitaryGroup_iff.mp g.2).2
    rw [hvg, det_toComplexMatrix, ← Complex.ofReal_one, Complex.ofReal_inj] at hdet
    exact hdet
  have hsqrt : (√2 : ℝ) ≠ 0 := (Real.sqrt_pos.mpr zero_lt_two).ne'
  have h2re : 2 * q.re = (v 0 : ℝ) * √2 := by
    simp only [q]
    field_simp
    rw [Real.sq_sqrt zero_le_two]
    ring
  have hv0 : v 0 = 0 ∨ v 0 ^ 2 = 1 :=
    (by decide : ∀ v ∈ binaryOctahedralCosetCoords, v 0 = 0 ∨ v 0 ^ 2 = 1) v hv
  have h8 : 8 = 4 * 2 := rfl
  have hq8 : q ^ 8 = 1 := by
    rcases hv0 with h0 | hsq
    · have hq4 : q ^ 4 = 1 := by rw [pow_four_of_normSq_eq_one hq, h2re, h0]; ext <;> norm_num
      rw [h8, pow_mul, hq4, one_pow]
    · have hsq' : ((v 0 : ℝ) * √2) ^ 2 = 2 := by
        rw [mul_pow, Real.sq_sqrt zero_le_two, (by exact_mod_cast hsq : (v 0 : ℝ) ^ 2 = 1), one_mul]
      have hq4 : q ^ 4 = -1 := by rw [pow_four_of_normSq_eq_one hq, h2re, hsq']; ext <;> norm_num
      rw [h8, pow_mul, hq4, neg_one_sq]
  apply Subtype.ext
  rw [SubmonoidClass.coe_pow, hvg, ← map_pow, hq8, map_one, OneMemClass.coe_one]

/-- Every element of `TauCeti.SU2.binaryOctahedralSubgroup` satisfies `g ^ 8 = 1` or `g ^ 6 = 1`. -/
theorem pow_eight_or_pow_six_eq_one_of_mem_binaryOctahedralSubgroup {g : SU2}
    (hg : g ∈ binaryOctahedralSubgroup) : g ^ 8 = 1 ∨ g ^ 6 = 1 := by
  rcases hg with hg | ⟨v, hv, hvg⟩
  · obtain ⟨v, hv, hvg⟩ := mem_binaryTetrahedralSubgroup_iff.mp hg
    exact pow_eight_or_pow_six_of_mem_binaryTetrahedralCoords hv hvg
  · exact .inl (pow_eight_of_mem_binaryOctahedralCosetCoords hv hvg)

/-- Every element of `TauCeti.SU2.binaryOctahedralSubgroup` has order dividing `8` or `6`. -/
theorem orderOf_dvd_eight_or_six_of_mem_binaryOctahedralSubgroup {g : SU2}
    (hg : g ∈ binaryOctahedralSubgroup) : orderOf g ∣ 8 ∨ orderOf g ∣ 6 := by
  rcases pow_eight_or_pow_six_eq_one_of_mem_binaryOctahedralSubgroup hg with h | h
  · exact .inl (orderOf_dvd_iff_pow_eq_one.mpr h)
  · exact .inr (orderOf_dvd_iff_pow_eq_one.mpr h)

/-- **Every element of the binary octahedral subgroup has order at most `8`.** -/
theorem orderOf_le_eight_of_mem_binaryOctahedralSubgroup {g : SU2}
    (hg : g ∈ binaryOctahedralSubgroup) : orderOf g ≤ 8 := by
  rcases orderOf_dvd_eight_or_six_of_mem_binaryOctahedralSubgroup hg with h | h
  · exact Nat.le_of_dvd (by norm_num) h
  · exact (Nat.le_of_dvd (by norm_num) h).trans (by norm_num)

/-- **The binary octahedral subgroup is not cyclic** (distinguishing it from the cyclic subgroup of
order 48). -/
theorem not_isCyclic_binaryOctahedralSubgroup : ¬ IsCyclic binaryOctahedralSubgroup := by
  intro hcyc
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := IsCyclic.exists_ofOrder_eq_natCard (α := binaryOctahedralSubgroup)
  have hle := orderOf_le_eight_of_mem_binaryOctahedralSubgroup g.2
  rw [Subgroup.orderOf_coe, hg, natCard_binaryOctahedralSubgroup] at hle
  omega

/-- **The binary octahedral subgroup is not isomorphic to any dicyclic group `QuaternionGroup n`**
(in particular distinguishing it from `QuaternionGroup 12` of order 48). -/
theorem isEmpty_mulEquiv_quaternionGroup (n : ℕ) :
    IsEmpty (binaryOctahedralSubgroup ≃* QuaternionGroup n) := by
  refine ⟨fun e => ?_⟩
  have hord : orderOf (e.symm (QuaternionGroup.a 1)) = 2 * n :=
    (orderOf_injective e.symm.toMonoidHom e.symm.injective (QuaternionGroup.a 1)).trans
      QuaternionGroup.orderOf_a_one
  rcases eq_zero_or_neZero n with rfl | hn
  · exact (orderOf_pos (e.symm (QuaternionGroup.a 1))).ne' hord
  · have hcard : 48 = 4 * n := by
      rw [← natCard_binaryOctahedralSubgroup, Nat.card_congr e.toEquiv,
        Nat.card_eq_fintype_card, QuaternionGroup.card]
    have hle := orderOf_le_eight_of_mem_binaryOctahedralSubgroup (e.symm (QuaternionGroup.a 1)).2
    rw [Subgroup.orderOf_coe, hord] at hle
    omega

end TauCeti.SU2
